33:      $ gbs build -A i586   # build all packages under current dir for i586
34:      $ gbs build -A armv7l # build all packages under current dir for armv7l
35:      $ gbs build -A i586 --overwrite   # rebuild the packages
36:      $ gbs build -A i586 --include-all # build packages including un-commit changes
37:      $ gbs build -A i586 --incremental # incremental build
38:      $ gbs build -A i586 --noinit      # build with offline mode
39:      $ gbs build -A i586 --clean       # clean build by deleting the old build root
40:      $ gbs build -A i586 <gitdir>      # build all packages under <gitdir>
45:  gitdir                git repository path, which can contain multiple
52:build configuration options:
53:  -A ARCH, --arch ARCH  build target arch. Supported arch types are: x86_64
54:                        i586 armv6l armv7hl armv7l aarch64 aarch64ilp32
55:                        aarch64_ilp32 mips mipsel riscv32 riscv64
56:  -D DIST, --dist DIST  specify project (build) configuration file. User can
57:                        specify build config in [profile.xx] section of
58:                        gbs.conf using 'buildconf' key, and the value is local
59:                        path of build conf file
61:                        profile to be used for building, it is defined in
62:                        .gbs.conf, can be given without the "profile." prefix
63:  -R REPOSITORIES, --repository REPOSITORIES
64:                        specify package repositories, only rpm-md format is
66:  --skip-conf-repos     skip repositories mentioned in config file, and only
67:                        use repos from command line -R option
68:  --overwrite           overwrite existing binaries and build them anyway
70:  --debug               debug output
71:  --baselibs            create -32bit/-64bit/-x86 rpms for other architectures
73:build env options:
74:  -B BUILDROOT, --buildroot BUILDROOT
75:                        specify build root to setup chroot environment. By
77:                        customized build root in gbs.conf with 'buildroot'
79:                        build root, or in [profile.xx] section for profile
80:                        special build root
81:  -C, --clean           delete old build root before initialization
82:  --clean-once          clean the build environment only once when you start
83:                        building multiple packages, after that use existing
85:  --clean-repos         clean up local repos created by gbs build before
86:                        building packages
87:  --fail-fast           stop build if one of packages fails
89:                        If a package build fails, do not abort and
90:                        continuebuilding other packages in the queue
92:                        specify extra packages to install to build root,
94:  --keep-packs          keep unused packages in build root. without this
95:                        option, unused packages will be removed from build
96:                        root
97:  --use-higher-deps     Which repo provides higher version deps, use it
98:  --kvm                 Launch a kvm machine to build package instead of using
99:                        chroot
110:  --not-export-source   Do not export source, use git source to build directly
111:  --full-build          Download all the package sources except local package
112:                        in gbs.conf, and do build
113:  --deps-build          Download packages depends on local package from
114:                        gbs.conf, and do build
116:  --failures-to-rebuild FAILURES_TO_REBUILD
117:                        Specify the failure list of build, if the package
118:                        build fails and the failure is in the list, the
121:  --rebuild-count REBUILD_COUNT
122:                        The rebuild count of package which depended on
123:                        --failures-to-rebuild
125:speed up building options:
126:  --incremental         build a package from the local git tree incremental.
127:                        If the build fails, changes can be done directly to
128:                        the source and build can continue from where it
130:  --no-configure        this option disables running configure scripts and
132:                        build possible. This requires the configure scripts in
133:                        the spec to be referenced using the %configure,
134:                        %reconfigure and %autogen macros
135:  --noinit              working in offline mode. Start building directly
136:  --ccache              use ccache to speed up rebuilds
139:                        ccache.tar file to speed up rebuilds
140:  --icecream ICECREAM   Use N parallel build jobs with icecream
141:  --threads THREADS     number of threads to build multiple packages in
143:  --skip-srcrpm         don't build source rpm file
147:                        specify a commit ID to build
148:  --include-all         uncommitted changes and untracked files would be
174:  --worktree WORKTREE   specify git worktree directory path(s) to build.
199:  --exclude EXCLUDE     specify a package list to be excluded for building.
201:  --exclude-from-file EXCLUDE_FROM_FILE
202:                        specify an exclude package list text file, the format
206:  --deps                build specified packages and all packages they depend
207:                        on, such as A depends B,C,D, first build B,C,D and
208:                        then build A
209:  --rdeps               build specified packages and all packages depend on
210:                        them, such as A B C depends D, first build D and then
211:                        build A,B,C
212:  --disable-debuginfo   Do not create debuginfo packages when building
214:  --export-only         only export, not building
